/ninebot-ble/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock

# JNI Libraries
#
# Generated, not committed.
#
# These .so files used to be checked in, which is what allowed them to drift
# away from the Rust sources: the APK packaged whatever binary was committed,
# and nothing compared it to the code. A protocol or crypto fix in ninebot-ble
# could sit in the tree for months without ever reaching a build.
#
# The `copyRustJniLibs` Gradle task now regenerates them from source on every
# build and writes a content-hash stamp; `verifyRustJniLibs` fails the build if
# the libraries are missing or do not match the sources. See app/build.gradle.kts.
#
# To build without a Rust toolchain: ./gradlew assembleDebug -PskipRustBuild
/app/src/main/jniLibs/

